00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:20.990
The fact that we have unified
API and very consistent

00:03:20.990 --> 00:03:24.170
latencies across all
different storage classes

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:30.030
helps a great deal when you use
GCS for different use cases.

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:32.720
So with us you don't have to
use a different API if you

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:34.880
are talking to the
cold storage tier,

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:37.220
or you don't have
to think of how

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:39.350
do I architect a system
for offline latencies,

00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:42.080
because for us every
storage class has

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:45.260
online latencies-- consistent
subsequent latencies.

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:46.590
GCS is very reliable.

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:49.790
GCS is very cost effective
across all different storage

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:50.840
classes.

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:54.360
And last but not the
least, and in this session

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:56.690
